{"name":"Blue Smart","hex":"#5786b4","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"smart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hurt or sting.","To cause a smart or sting in."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Exhibiting social ability or cleverness.","Exhibiting intellectual knowledge, such as that found in books."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Smart (marque)","blocks":[{"text":"Smart is a Swiss born-German automotive marque established in 1994 and currently operating as Smart Automobile Co., Ltd., a joint venture formed in 2019 by Mercedes-Benz AG and Zhejiang Geely Holding Group, aimed at manufacturing Smart-badged cars in China to be marketed globally. The venture is headquartered in Ningbo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Smart_2022.svg/330px-Smart_2022.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smart_(marque)","wikidata":"Q156490"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Smart_Verwaltungszentrale_B%C3%B6blingen_04.jpg/500px-Smart_Verwaltungszentrale_B%C3%B6blingen_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Smart_Verwaltungszentrale_B%C3%B6blingen_04.jpg/1280px-Smart_Verwaltungszentrale_B%C3%B6blingen_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Smart_Verwaltungszentrale_B%C3%B6blingen_04.jpg/500px-Smart_Verwaltungszentrale_B%C3%B6blingen_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Former Smart offices in Böblingen","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmart_Verwaltungszentrale_B%C3%B6blingen_04.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Smart-Hambach02.jpg/500px-Smart-Hambach02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Smart-Hambach02.jpg/1280px-Smart-Hambach02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Smart-Hambach02.jpg/500px-Smart-Hambach02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Smart glass tower near Smartville, Hambach, in 2007","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmart-Hambach02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons